put for the particular sink before trusting it; enforce memory retention/deletion/privacy and trust on reads/writes; permit secret-bearing prompt/tool/provider/log disclosure only through explicit matching policy. Reject: Retrieved or tool content overriding privileged policy, unvalidated model output at a trusted sink, stale/deleted or cross-policy memory access, and unauthorized secret disclosure. Required outputs: Prompt provenance/role record, sink validation and taint result, memory policy/lifecycle evidence, redacted secret-policy denial diagnostics. Dependencies: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping ai/prompt-memory-boundary; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred. Criterion profile-gap/ai/replay-evaluation-artifacts (Open): Input: Agent execution with model/provider/prompt/tool/policy identities, review decisions, retry/error state and selected audit/replay mode. Accept: Emit the execution ledger with prompt/message and generated-code digests, tool inputs/outputs, review/policy/nondeterminism/error/retry records; replay required operations from matching records. Expose an evaluation hook that produces separately identified fixtures/results without granting authority. Reject: Replay/audit-required execution missing required records, digest or identity substitution, or evaluation results used to bypass capability/safety/review checks. Required outputs: Model/tool call trace, replay/audit log schema and records, generated-code digest, independently identified evaluation result. Dependencies: workflow, runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/connect-distributedai-replay-and-interactive-execution interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping ai/replay-evaluation-artifacts; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.\n\nCriterion `domain/support-agent-integration`: Execute and evaluate declared support triage with prompt provenance, structured-output/taint, durable graph/replay, tool policy and required refund/review transitions. Accepted fixture: Run support triage with prompt provenance, structured validated outputs, retrieval trust, durable replay, tool policy and explicit refund human-review transition. Negative fixture: Reject prompt policy escalation, unvalidated output, missing tool grant or write tool without required review. Required evidence: agent/tool/prompt/memory/review graph, eval and replay reports; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume schema, workflow outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource-qualified acceptance: Source obligation `language/facet/emit-agent-plan`: Emit an agent facet's prompt/tool/model/evaluation/trace/guardrail artifacts with explicit model/tool effects and capabilities. Accept: Compile an explicitly activated agent facet into prompt artifacts, tool schemas, model-call declarations, evaluation hooks, trace requirements and guardrail checks; retain model/tool effects and capabilities without hidden runtime privilege. The SupportAgent example is an artifact-generation fixture, not authorization for live calls. Reject: Reject missing prompt/tool/model/evaluation/trace/guardrail products, inactive/unsupported facet use or authority inferred from prompt text. Required outputs: Versioned source-bound agent artifact bundle and accepted fixture plus missing-product/effect/grant rejection diagnostics. Dependencies consume versioned facts/receipts from expand/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/expand5-integrate-generated-programs, effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects3-check-legality-and-ordering, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime; they do not require blanket component completion. Implementation status remains Open."}
