   "No externally visible operation after denial; explicit grant provenance end to end. For SAFE10/SAFE13/SAFE14, execute service-boundary allowed/denied fixtures with provider presence/scope, typed error or declared panic and required audit/telemetry; redact secrets. Tool schema checks, side-effect class and human-review policy must precede invocation; package/build authority cannot silently become runtime grants. A compiler authorization record alone is insufficient runtime enforcement evidence. Criterion behavior/pkg6/request-grant-separation: accept Deploy only scoped handles for capabilities requested by the package and allowed by deployment policy; keep source requests, package requests, denials and actual grants distinct. Reject A dependency grants authority, a deployment grants an unrequested capability, or a runtime effect uses ambient authority instead of its scoped handle. Emit Package-to-deployment grant/handle provenance and PKG6005/PKG6006 before the effect. Dependencies: L15, SAFE10, PKG6, R11. Criterion behavior/pkg6/transitive-deny-precedence: accept Check every source-analysis/project/manifest/resolver/deployment/runtime edge; explicit denials remain effective across transitive dependency requests. Reject Any required edge is missing, a transitive request overrides denial, or an action/build proceeds despite conflicting policy. Emit Authority-chain decision with dependency chain/effect/capability/grant source/policy and PKG6004. Dependencies: PKG6, PKG5, SAFE10, R11. Allocation decision/runtime-schema-safe10-strengthening (Open). Role: auth owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: the actual current dependency/consumer record and proposed older-to-current source field transpose. Required positive predicate: When transposing older Runtime/Schema bindings, preserve the later strengthened SAFE10 operation gate and its current qualification; never overwrite it with an older whole record. Positive output witness: Current provider/scope/phase operation-gate decision at the actual runtime/build sink and a prefix-preserving field transpose. Concrete negative case: An older Runtime/Schema whole record overwrites the strengthened SAFE10 operation gate, admitting an external effect after denial or dropping grant/provider/schema/phase provenance. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred.",
