   "Real allowed operation and denied widening/revoked/wrong-phase operations. Enforce [SAFE10](../../docs/phase-02-safety/039-safe10-capability-security-model.md) intersection across source/function, package/dependency, workspace, profile, invocation/deployment and runtime scope. Reject undeclared ambient authority and forbidden declared ambient contexts; check each capability family's scope. Record parent/derived attenuation and lifetime without expansion; enforce provider-specific revocation or reject unsupported requirements unless a static lifetime substitute is valid. Separate build/runtime secrets and prevent public diagnostic, generated-code, cache-key and artifact leakage. Actual external model billing policy remains separate from removed project accounting. Decision criterion interface/profile/narrow-authority: Check effect allowance and capability authorization as distinct typed predicates narrowed by source/profile/package/provider/deployment policy; missing declarations deny, and no narrower layer is widened. Reject: Reject missing/widened authority and wrong-phase/lifetime grants; do not literally intersect effect labels with differently typed capability names without the declared provider mapping. Required outputs: Effect permission, capability/grant/provider mapping and denial records, narrowing/default-deny and phase/lifetime refusal fixtures. Allocation interface/safety/safe10/ambient-policy (Open). Role: auth owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: authority-bearing operation with separately typed requirements, grants, provider, scope and phase. Required positive predicate: Reject undeclared ambient authority and forbid even declared ambient contexts when profile/policy disallows them. Positive output witness: Ambient declaration and profile/policy admission or denial before the authority-bearing operation. Concrete negative case: Undeclared ambient filesystem/network/secret authority is used, or a forbidden profile accepts even a declared ambient context. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe10/attenuation (Open). Role: auth owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: authority-bearing operation with separately typed requirements, grants, provider, scope and phase. Required positive predicate: Narrow capability scope/lifetime only, recording parent/derived identity and never adding authority where attenuation is supported. Positive output witness: Parent/derived capability identities, narrowed scope/lifetime and nonexpansion evidence. Concrete negative case: A derived capability broadens parent paths, actions, lifetime or scope rather than narrowing it. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe10/grant-intersection (Open). Role: auth owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: authority-bearing operation with separately typed requirements, grants, provider, scope and phase. Required positive predicate: Require capability/grant/provider for authority-bearing operations; compute effective scope by intersecting source, function/effect, package/dependency, workspace, profile, invocation/deployment and runtime policy without child expansion. Positive output witness: Separately typed capability requirements, grants, provider and effective policy-layer intersection with denial provenance. Concrete negative case: A dependency or runtime scope expands source/package/workspace/profile/invocation authority, or effect labels are used as grants. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe10/revocation (Open). Role: auth owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: authority-bearing operation with separately typed requirements, grants, provider, scope and phase. Required positive predicate: Enforce provider-declared revoker, post-revocation failure, threading and synchronous behavior; reject required unsupported revocation unless static lifetime substitutes. Positive output witness: Revoker/post-revocation error/threading/synchronous contract, or a valid static lifetime substitute/refusal. Concrete negative case: Revoked authority continues to authorize an operation or an API requires provider revocation semantics that are unsupported. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinar