   "Actual published package retrieval/verification fixtures; tamper and missing-record rejection. SAFE14 verifies registry digest/signature/manifest/attestation before use; generated outputs retain generator/version, source/output digests, effects/grants, reproducibility and performed safety checks. Safe package claims require reproducibility or accepted provenance attestations, not registry identity alone. SAFE15 certificate imports verify matching package, compiler/schema, profile/target, provider trust and noninvalidated assumptions before use. Exercise registry accept, reject and quarantine decisions under declared policy. Reject missing identity, owner, provenance, SBOM, hashes, capability/profile/target metadata or required signatures and conformance reports. Expose unsafe, AI, FFI and host-delegation surfaces before installation; reject hidden authority, malicious releases and unmitigated dependency confusion. Validate stable identity/namespace/owner/version/license metadata, declared policy/signing status, manifest/lock where applicable, hashes/provenance/SBOM, profile/target matrices and conformance reports tied to compiler/target/profile/stdlib versions. Expose effects/capabilities, unsafe GOV9 metadata, FFI/host delegation and AI policy/eval/human-review/prompt-injection evidence before publication/use. Apply declared reproducibility/signature/license/security/malware/dependency-confusion policy with accept/reject/quarantine outcomes; namespace and emergency decisions are consumed, not invented by the gate. Reject incomplete/unsigned-when-required/nonreproducible/malicious/authority-hidden releases, missing provenance/SBOM/hashes, unsupported conformance claims and unmitigated dependency confusion. Reject policy-forbidden advisory/yanked dependencies and reserved-name abuse; quarantine unresolved security/provenance risk according to policy. Criterion behavior/pkg10/keyless-provenance-verification: accept Verify keyless issuer/subject/audience, certificate identity/validity, trusted root and transparency inclusion evidence against the exact provenance subject under identity/freshness policy. Reject A required identity/certificate/root/log proof is absent, unverifiable, stale or policy-incompatible. Emit Keyless identity/log verification and PKG10009/PKG10010. Dependencies: PKG10, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg10/model-generated-source-taint: accept Mark model-generated code/patches as generated, retain generator/input lineage, and recheck through normal compiler and applicable review gates before removing taint. Reject Generated source is untracked, loses generator/input identity or becomes trusted before its checks succeed. Emit Generated-source ledger, compiler/review result linkage and PKG10004. Dependencies: PKG10, A11, C1. Criterion behavior/pkg10/release-provenance-artifact: accept Emit canonical schema-valid provenance for the exact subject/content with source/repository/project/lock/compiler/builder/platform/recipe/dependency/generator/blob/test/safety/rebuild/signature/SBOM/advisory identities and active policy. Reject Required provenance/lock summaries, generator or blob source/hash/license/policy fields, artifact links or required identity-based signer evidence are missing or mismatched. Emit Provenance, builder/keyless/log attestations, generated/blob/dependency ledgers, revocation/verification report and release decision; PKG10001/PKG10002/PKG10004/PKG10005/PKG10007. Dependencies: PKG3, PKG5, PKG7, PKG8, PKG10, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg10/revoked-provenance-admission: accept Check consumed package/builder/signature/attestation revocation under release policy, preserving the explicitly permitted historical rebuild exception. Reject A revoked input is accepted without that exact historical exception. Emit Revocation report and release refusal/exception with PKG10006. Dependencies: PKG10, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg10/trusted-builder-admission: accept Verify builder identity, declared platform and required build evidence before accepting a trusted release provenance claim. Reject A release builder is unknown or cannot satisfy the active builder trust policy. Emit Verified builder attestation or PKG10003 with builder/subject/policy identity. Dependencies: PKG10, GOV4. Criterion behavior/pkg10/unknown-provenance-schema-denial: accept Consume only provenance schemas and required trust fields that the release verifier can validate. Reject An unknown schema or unvalidated required trust field is accepted optimistically. Emit Schema verification denial with PKG10008. Dependencies: PKG10, S9. Criterion behavior/pkg12/evidence-backed-attestation-level: accept Evaluate baseline/tracked/isolated/hermetic/reproducible/certified policy levels and selected verification track against their explicit builder/material/isolation/input/rebuild/governance/conformance evidence. Reject A required level/track is downgraded or isolation/hermetic/reproducible claims lack evidence and declared exceptions. Emit Level/track and consumer-gate decision; PKG12013/PKG12016. Dependencies: PKG12, PKG7, GOV4, GOV10. Criterion behavior/pkg12/keyless-trust-verification: accept Verify artifact subject/signature, OIDC issuer/subject/audience/claims, SAN/certificate validity at signing, chain/root-update trust, revocation and policy-required log inclusion/time/checkpoint/consistency evidence. Reject Any required identity/certificate/root/log/timestamp proof is missing, stale, revoked, mismatched, unverifiable or policy-incompatible. Emit Keyless identity/root/log verification bundle and PKG12014/PKG12017-PKG12020, without exposing signing secrets. Dependencies: PKG12, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg12/provenance-subject-binding: accept Bind the signed attestation to exact artifact subject/manifest and builder/signing/platform/source/revision/archive/generated/patch/lock/dependency/compiler/toolchain/recipe identity with timestamps, exceptions and gate metadata. Reject The subject mismatches or required builder/platform/source/lock/recipe information is absent. Emit Canonical attestation payload/hash and verification report; PKG12009-PKG12012. Dependencies: PKG12, PKG10, PKG7. Criterion behavior/pkg12/revoked-signing-admission: accept Check key/signature/package/provenance revocation and policy-scoped validity before release, admitting only an explicit policy-permitted historical rebuild. Reject Revoked or invalid signing material is accepted without the exact historical exception. Emit Revocation check and release verification decision; PKG12006. Dependencies: PKG12, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg12/transitive-sbom: accept Emit all transitive package/artifact dependencies with version/source/hash/registry/license/capability/privileged/unsafe/FFI/blob/generated/provenance/advisory/revocation metadata using Gravity's canonical schema. Reject A transitive dependency or an applicable capability/unsafe/generated/blob field is missing. Emit SBOM and validation report with PKG12004/PKG12005. Dependencies: PKG12, PKG5, PKG6, PKG8. Criterion behavior/pkg12/verification-report: accept Record every performed/failed verification check with artifact/signature/signer/SBOM/dependency/attestation/builder/platform/source/time/root/log/policy/track identity while redacting secrets. Reject A report omits a failed check, hides its evidence/policy context or discloses protected signing/package data. Emit Verification, attestation, SBOM, revocation, freshness, policy and consumer-decision artifacts; PKG12008. Dependencies: PKG12, C15. Criterion behavior/pkg12/verify-before-consumption: accept Run required schema/content/signature/provenance/attestation/SBOM/safety/revocation/freshness/identity/level/track/policy checks successfully before consumer use. Reject Consumer use precedes verification or mandatory evidence is missing, unsigned, stale, revoked, mismatched or policy-incompatible. Emit Consumer acceptance/denial with complete failed-check report and PKG12001/PKG12003/PKG12007/PKG12009/PKG12015/PKG12016. Dependencies: PKG12, PKG3, PKG10. Criterion behavior/pkg2/build-release-evidence: accept Produce per-target artifacts with required graph, test, safety, provenance, signature and SBOM evidence under the release policy. Reject A required release-evidence record is missing or passing the host default is used instead of the required target matrix. Emit Build graph/node and conformance records, recipe, provenance, signatures/SBOM and PKG2005/PKG2006. Dependencies: PKG3, PKG7, PKG11, TEST1, TEST13. Criterion behavior/pkg3/artifact-manifest: accept Emit schema-valid manifests for every artifact kind with canonical kind/schema/package/source/project/lock/compiler/profile/target/policy/content/dependency/evidence identity, generator inputs and conditional authority/safety/release links. Reject A manifest/schema/kind/identity/generator or required authority/safety/provenance/signature/SBOM link is missing, unknown or noncanonical. Emit Artifact and schema/kind registries, canonical identity/manifest and positive/negative fixtures; PKG3001-PKG3008. Dependencies: S3, S9, B13, PKG10, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg3/consumer-artifact-admission: accept Verify schema compatibility, actual content identity and required evidence before artifact use. Reject A consumer ignores a required evidence link, unknown schema version or content mismatch. Emit Consumer acceptance/denial record and PKG3002/PKG3004/PKG3005/PKG3008. Dependencies: PKG3, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg4/download-verification: accept Verify the downloaded content hash and registry signature when policy requires it before installation or consumption. Reject Installation or consumption proceeds after hash/signature verification is absent or fails. Emit Package verification report and PKG4001 naming package/version/registry/operation. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg4/offline-install: accept Install from a complete lockfile and local content/verification cache without network effects. Reject Offline installation attempts fetches or succeeds with an incomplete cache/lockfile. Emit Structured offline operation/verification decision and PKG4006. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG5, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg4/package-operation-artifacts: accept Expose add/remove/update/resolve/fetch/verify/audit/explain/publish/yank/mirror/vendor with declared filesystem/network/plugin effects and structured inputs/outputs/registry/signature/lock changes. Reject An operation hides a policy-relevant diff in prose-only logs or a plugin executes an undeclared effect. Emit Machine/human operation records, lock/metadata/verification/capability/safety/provenance/access/publish/yank artifacts and PKG4005. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG6, PKG8, PKG9. Criterion behavior/pkg4/package-update-diff: accept Present dependency/version, capability, unsafe, target, license and provenance changes for review before mutating project/lock state. Reject An update adds authority without required policy review or hides a policy-relevant change. Emit Structured lock/capability/unsafe/target/license/provenance diff and PKG4003. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG6, PKG8. Criterion behavior/pkg4/publication-verification: accept Publish only after project/artifact manifest, signature, SBOM and release-policy verification succeeds. Reject Publication proceeds without policy-required signature, SBOM or other release evidence. Emit Verification and publish decision records with PKG4004. Dependencies: PKG1, PKG3, PKG4, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg4/registry-token-redaction: accept Treat registry authentication tokens as secrets and redact them from both human and machine operation output. Reject A credential appears in a log, diagnostic, operation record or artifact. Emit Redacted access/operation records and PKG4007 without the secret. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG9. Criterion behavior/pkg4/yank-history: accept Yank changes selection policy while preserving metadata needed to rebuild existing lockfiles. Reject Yanking erases historical content/identity metadata needed for a locked rebuild. Emit Yank record, retained metadata and PKG4008. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG5, PKG7. Criterion behavior/pkg6/capability-update-diff: accept Expose dependency update changes to effect/capability and unsafe surfaces before acceptance. Reject Transitive capability expansion or changed unsafe assumptions bypass policy review. Emit Effect/capability update diff and PKG6003. Dependencies: PKG4, PKG6. Criterion behavior/pkg8/package-safety-metadata: accept Emit schema-valid unsafe/island/safe-wrapper/FFI ABI-ownership-lifetime-error/privileged/taint/proof-checker/test/reviewer/advisory/exception metadata linked to required lock/SBOM/artifact records. Reject Unsafe or taint surfaces are hidden, wrapper evidence or FFI assumptions are missing, proof/checker links are absent, or metadata is schema-invalid. Emit Safety manifest, island/FFI/taint/proof indexes, review state, update diff and gate evidence; PKG8001-PKG8005. Dependencies: SAFE6, SAFE7, SAFE11, SAFE15, PKG8. Criterion behavior/pkg8/revoked-safety-invalidation: accept Invalidate dependent release gates when consumed safety/proof/review inputs become revoked or quarantined. Reject A revoked proof claim or quarantined dependency still satisfies the release gate. Emit Revocation/quarantine dependency decision with PKG8006/PKG8008. Dependencies: PKG8, SAFE15. Criterion behavior/pkg8/safety-update-diff: accept Show changed safety metadata, assumptions and affected claims in the package update diff. Reject A package update changes safety/FFI/unsafe/proof assumptions without surfacing them for policy review. Emit Safety diff and PKG8007. Dependencies: PKG8, PKG4. Criterion behavior/pkg8/unreviewed-unsafe-admission: accept Preserve unreviewed/reviewed/requires-recheck/quarantined/revoked/accepted-exception states and apply the exact release/deployment policy for each. Reject An unreviewed unsafe package is released without matching policy or scoped exception, or quarantine/revocation is ignored. Emit Review-state table and explicit release gate/exception decision. Dependencies: PKG8, SAFE6. Criterion behavior/pkg9/generated-candidate-provenance: accept Record a generated candidate's generator identity and input hashes before any review/publish transition. Reject Generated candidates lack provenance or unreviewed generated source becomes implicitly trusted. Emit Generator/provenance record and PKG9005. Dependencies: PKG9, PKG10, A11. Criterion behavior/pkg9/latent-package-state: accept Track reserved/generated/review-requested/reviewed/published/rejected/revoked transitions; published resolves normally and other states require explicit grants and matching policy. Reject Latent names satisfy ordinary constraints or a candidate is published without its required reviewed transition. Emit Latent-state transition, access and publish decisions; PKG9004/PKG9006. Dependencies: PKG9, GOV10. Criterion behavior/pkg9/mirror-authenticity: accept Verify and preserve original registry signatures or emit a verifiable mirror attestation for mirrored content. Reject A mirror loses original signatures and cannot provide a verifying attestation. Emit Mirror state/attestation/verification record and PKG9007. Dependencies: PKG9, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg9/registry-access-privacy: accept Require private read authorization before returning metadata and produce public errors that do not reveal private package existence. Reject An ungranted principal reads private metadata or learns private existence from public resolution errors. Emit Privacy-safe access decision with registry/package/principal scope and PKG9001/PKG9002. Dependencies: PKG9, L15. Criterion behavior/pkg9/registry-history-retention: accept Retain yank/revocation records and identity/material required for policy-authorized reproducible historical builds. Reject Registry mutation erases retained historical rebuild evidence or silently hides revocation state. Emit Registry yank/revocation log, retained provenance and historical build decision. Dependencies: PKG9, PKG7, GOV10. Criterion behavior/pkg9/registry-index-verification: accept Verify registry indexes when signatures are required and record the registry source in every selected package lock record. Reject Required index signatures fail/are absent or a selected lock record omits its registry source. Emit Index signature/source verification and PKG9003/PKG9008. Dependencies: PKG9, PKG5, PKG12. Criterion behavior/pkg9/registry-publication-gate: accept Publish only with preserved provenance/safety metadata and the policy-required review/state transition. Reject A private/latent publish bypasses required review or loses safety/provenance metadata. Emit Publish/state/provenance decision and PKG9006. Dependencies: PKG9, PKG8, PKG10, GOV10. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/generated-provenance (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Reject generated package artifacts lacking generator/source/output digests, effects/grants, reproducibility status and performed safety checks. Positive output witness: Generator/source/output provenance, reproducibility and performed-check records. Concrete negative case: Generated source/schema/native/proof artifacts lack generator/version, input/output digests, effects/grants or performed safety checks. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred. Allocation interface/safety/safe14/pinned-trust (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Pin safe/release dependency and generated/replay/compiler/provider/facet/grant provenance and verify registry signatures/digests/manifests/attestations; safe claims require reproducible builds or accepted attestations. Positive output witness: Verified lock/provenance chain and reproducible build or accepted attestation evidence. Concrete negative case: Safe/release resolution lacks a pinned package/provider/facet/compiler/grant/generated/replay record or accepts registry identity without digest/signature/attestation checks. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred.",
