   "Real use-after-move, escape, invalid borrow and linear-resource fixtures with graphs. Consume the [SAFE2-SAFE5 contracts](plan.md): partial initialization drops only initialized fields; disjoint borrows require range proof; calls expose copy/move/borrow/consume behavior; region exit and arena reset invalidate dependent references; reject foreign retention and detached captures without lifetime proof. Demonstrate provider-specific exactly-once terminal cleanup on normal, exceptional, panic, cancellation, timeout and early-return paths, including generated linear duplication rejection. Lease renewal versus terminal consumption remains a source qualification, not an inferred terminal event. Decision allocation interface/safety/safe3/borrow-exclusivity (Open). Role: ownership/borrow checker maintainer. Allow many immutable or one exclusive mutable borrow per range/lifetime; forbid moving or consuming borrowed owners and conflicting nested aliases, with only declared interior mutation or proved disjoint splitting. Refusals and conditional cases: Reject overlapping mutable/immutable or multiple mutable borrows, owner move/consumption while borrowed and conflicting nested aliases. Accept many immutable or one exclusive mutable borrow only for its valid range/lifetime, with interior mutation explicitly declared or disjoint splitting proved. Required outputs: Range/lifetime borrow graph, exclusivity proof, legal interior/disjoint fixtures and conflicting-borrow diagnostics. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed. Decision allocation interface/safety/safe3/ownership-move (Open). Role: ownership/borrow checker maintainer. Track ownership kinds and explicit moves/consumption; invalidate moved bindings and consumed aliases except persistent/copyable values or returned valid owners/borrows. Refusals and conditional cases: Reject use of moved bindings and consumed aliases; preserve copyable/persistent value legality and allow only valid returned owners/borrows under the declared ownership contract. Record each ownership kind and explicit copy/move/borrow/consume transition. Required outputs: Ownership state/transition graph, moved-binding invalidation and accepted exception/use-after-move refusal fixtures. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed. Decision allocation interface/safety/safe5/terminal-flow (Open). Role: linear resource checker maintainer. Track every acquired linear resource to exactly one contract-valid terminal operation on every modeled normal, exceptional, panic, cancellation, timeout and early exit path; reject leaks, duplicates, reuse and wrong-provider release. Refusals and conditional cases: Reject a leak, duplicate terminal operation, reuse after consumption, wrong-provider release or cleanup absent on any modeled normal/error/panic/cancellation/timeout/early-exit path. Require exactly one contract-valid terminal operation for every acquired linear resource; keep lease renewal versus terminal consumption as unresolved source qualification, not an invented terminal event. Required outputs: Provider-bound linear flow and per-path terminal-state report with accepted cleanup and leak/duplicate/reuse/wrong-provider diagnostics. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed. Decision criterion interface/language/concurrency/check-gpu-parallel-access: Require proof of device/shared-memory race freedom or valid synchronization before GPU parallel access; preserve address-space, ownership and barrier facts. Reject: Reject unproved unsynchronized access, invalid cross-space aliasing and missing or incompatible synchronization. Preserve unresolved finite18 facet identities pending authentic index recovery. Required outputs: Race/synchronization check and rejection records, plus a source-index adjudication identifying the actual spans/hashes of each retained unresolved facet ID. Decision criterion interface/language/memory/check-linear-resource-flow: Check exactly-once resource consumption or transfer and scoped acquisition/release; a privileged explicit forget path retains its declared policy boundary. Reject: Reject leaks, double consumption/release, invalid transfer and undeclared forget; preserve cleanup on every relevant normal/error/cancel path. Required outputs: Resource-flow and scope-cleanup graph, transfer/forget-policy evidence and leak/double-release refusal fixtures. Decision criterion interface/language/memory/check-owner-and-borrow-lifetimes: Check ownership moves, shared versus mutable borrows and region lifetimes; permit escape only by valid longer-lived transfer or explicit unsafe responsibility. Reject: Reject stale/moved owners, conflicting mutable borrows, invalid region captures and unaudited unsafe escape. Required outputs: Ownership/borrow/region graph, legal-transfer and invalid-use/escape fixtures, source-bound safety diagnostics."}
