   "Every dangerous operation classified and unclassified operations rejected. Under the [SAFE1/SAFE6-SAFE11/SAFE15 contracts](plan.md), inspect real checks before operations with defined profile-legal failure, complete unsafe audits even when permitted, wrapper preconditions and cleanup, source-bound review invalidation and dependency policy. Reject incomplete FFI contracts, unsupported atomics, implicit narrowing, undeclared relaxed numerics, taint loss, incompatible sanitizers and unvalidated deserialization; preserve residual taint and secret redaction. Emit inspectable outcome, proof, trust and audit records; internal-only unsafe boundaries confer no safe public API. Explicit wrapping/saturating conversions retain their unresolved relation to checked/proven narrowing. Runtime/provider execution and domain-specific consumers require their own evidence. P12: proof consumers check theorem/source/certificate/hash-chain/trusted-kernel/assumption/profile/target agreement; unverified imports are ignored or rejected only as policy states. Proof production and symbolic lowering are separate Math producer interfaces; a profile check alone cannot close them. Foundation requirement gravity/safety-family-conformance: Exercise each claimed safety family on accepted safe programs, rejected illegal programs and explicit audited unsafe-island cases; retain the applicable proven-safe, runtime-checked, rejected or unsafe-island outcome, owning diagnostics and evidence. Refusals: Reject an unclassified dangerous operation, hidden unsafe path, stale proof/audit or missing actual runtime-check failure case; no fifth implicit outcome or undefined safe behavior is allowed. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; pass-evidence - Actual subject-bound checker/proof/certificate/audit/replay/test evidence and verdicts. Foundation requirement gravity/unsafe-island-safe-api-eligibility: Expose unsafe-backed functionality as a safe API only when the wrapper proves or checks every required precondition and cleanup obligation, with source-bound audit and actual boundary tests; preserve internal-only status as a separate permitted boundary. Refusals: Reject invalid state escaping into safe code, a missing wrapper test/audit, an unproved precondition or treating internal-only unsafe code as a safe exported API. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-explicit-family-selection-and-no-runtime-rejection - Selected runtime/provider service contracts and actual link/load/service-use evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products. Decision allocation interface/safety/safe1/runtime-checks (Open). Role: compiler legality/safety maintainer. Emit required checks before unsafe behavior, with explicit conditions, declared profile-legal failure behavior, contexts and inspectable safety records. Refusals and conditional cases: Reject checks scheduled after the dangerous operation, absent condition/source/operation context, missing inspectable safety records or failure behavior illegal in the active profile. Exercise both passing and failing actual checks. Required outputs: Pre-operation runtime-check plan, condition/context/failure disposition and inspectable safety evidence. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed. Decision allocation interface/safety/safe1/safety-artifact (Open). Role: compiler legality/safety maintainer. Emit a consumable safety artifact connecting operations, outcomes, checks, unsafe islands, proofs, diagnostics, profile and mode for certificates and conformance consumers. Refusals and conditional cases: Reject an artifact missing operation/outcome/check/unsafe-island/proof/diagnostic/profile/safety-mode edges, or a certificate/conformance consumer unable to identify the exact classified subject. Required outputs: Consumable safety artifact linking operations, four outcomes, checks, unsafe islands, proofs, diagnostics, profile/mode and certificate/conformance input edges. Consume actual dependency interface outputs: pass-evidence, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-conformance-for-the-declared-profile-surface; whole-component completion is not a prerequisite. Retain exact source/compiler/pass/profile/target and checker/provider identities, actual positive products and refused-case diagnostics. Implementation acceptance remains unassessed. Decision criterion interface/language/memory/check-raw-and-mmio-boundary: Admit raw/MMIO operations only through explicit unsafe responsibility or an audited proved/runtime-checked safe wrapper, retaining address-space/width/alignment/volatile/order/grant semantics. Reject: Reject unclassified danger, ungranted device authority, invalid register shape/order and raw operations masquerading as ordinary safe code. Required outputs: Safe-wrapper/unsafe audit and device-map records, proof/check preservation and valid/invalid raw/MMIO diagnostics."}
