   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe11/deserialization (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: tainted source-to-sink flow with category set, validator, residual constraints and authority. Required positive predicate: Keep decoded data tainted until schema/content validation, reject arbitrary code/host-object deserialization and preserve field/unknown-key/default/binary taint facts. Positive output witness: Deserialization schema verdict and field/unknown-key/default/buffer taint facts. Concrete negative case: Decoded arbitrary code/host objects are accepted as safe data before schema/content validation, or unknown/default/binary fields lose taint. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
