   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe11/prompt-tool (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: tainted source-to-sink flow with category set, validator, residual constraints and authority. Required positive predicate: Treat model output and prompts as tainted, validate schema and authority before tool execution and mediate untrusted instruction roles through policy at privileged boundaries. Positive output witness: Prompt-role/taint separation, structured-output validation and capability/policy mediation at the actual sink. Concrete negative case: Untrusted retrieved/model/tool text is promoted into privileged instructions or unvalidated tool arguments. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
