   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe11/sink-enforcement (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: tainted source-to-sink flow with category set, validator, residual constraints and authority. Required positive predicate: Gate sensitive sinks on accepted taint state and required validation/encoding/parameterization/authority, preferring structured parameters and rejecting string-built query syntax without domain proof. Positive output witness: Source-to-sink flow, exact validator/encoder/parameterizer and capability decision. Concrete negative case: Tainted text is concatenated into SQL/shell/tool syntax without the required structural parameterization or sink proof. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
