   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe11/taint-source (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: tainted source-to-sink flow with category set, validator, residual constraints and authority. Required positive predicate: Mark untrusted values with multi-category taint, origin and trust boundary across runtime and build inputs; clearing one category leaves others unless declared relation permits it. Positive output witness: Category-set/origin/trust-boundary facts across runtime and build sources with independently retained categories. Concrete negative case: A multi-category untrusted input loses origin/trust boundary or clearing UserInput silently clears Secret/AIOutput as well. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
