   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe14/build-authority (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Deny hidden build/postinstall/network/shell/environment/model/tool/IR/native/registry activity by default; permitted effects require grants/providers/scopes/traces and hermetic releases require replayable effects or pinned outputs. Positive output witness: Build provider/scope/grant/trace and replay/pinned-output decision before the external effect. Concrete negative case: A package performs undeclared postinstall/network/shell/environment/model/tool/IR/native/registry work or an unreplayable hermetic effect. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
