   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe14/pinned-trust (Open). Role: build owning producer or consuming-boundary checker. Input: package resolution/build/update input with manifests, locks, dependencies and generated outputs. Required positive predicate: Pin safe/release dependency and generated/replay/compiler/provider/facet/grant provenance and verify registry signatures/digests/manifests/attestations; safe claims require reproducible builds or accepted attestations. Positive output witness: Verified lock/provenance chain and reproducible build or accepted attestation evidence. Concrete negative case: Safe/release resolution lacks a pinned package/provider/facet/compiler/grant/generated/replay record or accepts registry identity without digest/signature/attestation checks. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/bind-compiler-decisions-to-runtimebuild-enforcement-hooks supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-safe-code-classification-and-taintunsafe-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
