   :id "interface/safety/safe15/import-verification",
   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe15/import-verification (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: subject-bound safety proof/certificate with assumptions, method/provider, trust and invalidation inputs. Required positive predicate: Before using imported theorems or certificates, verify the statement/input/package and hash-chain identities, compiler/schema compatibility, assumptions, profile/target applicability and trusted-kernel or provider-signature evidence required by the governing proof contract. Failed imports are ignored or rejected by policy, never silently accepted. Positive output witness: Import compatibility/trust/current-applicability check and declared ignore-or-reject outcome, never silent acceptance. Concrete negative case: An imported certificate has mismatched statement/input/package/hash chain/compiler/schema/profile/target/assumptions or untrusted provider/kernel. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
