   :id "interface/safety/safe15/invalidation",
   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe15/invalidation (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: subject-bound safety proof/certificate with assumptions, method/provider, trust and invalidation inputs. Required positive predicate: Invalidate/regenerate affected certificates across source, expansion, type/effect, profile/target/mode/provider/pass/backend/dependency/grant/replay changes and force rechecking when mappings cannot survive. Positive output witness: Assumption mapping, changed or revoked dependency invalidation, regenerated proof/restored check or rejection and downstream applicability. Concrete negative case: A certificate survives source/type/effect/profile/target/mode/provider/pass/backend/dependency/grant/replay changes or revoked supporting trust without rechecking. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
