   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe15/wrapper-certificates (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: subject-bound safety proof/certificate with assumptions, method/provider, trust and invalidation inputs. Required positive predicate: Use certificates for unsafe wrappers only when exact wrapper invariants are proved under active profile/target and linked to SAFE6 audits. Positive output witness: Exact wrapper-invariant certificate, active profile/target applicability and linked SAFE6 audit. Concrete negative case: A certificate proves another wrapper invariant or profile/target but is used to expose the unsafe wrapper as safe. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
