   :id "interface/safety/safe16/optimization-backend",
   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe16/optimization-backend (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: claimed-profile safety corpus, actual compiler diagnostics/artifacts and target execution or explicit unavailable status. Required positive predicate: Compile checks-retained and optimized fixture modes and verify proof-backed erasure and backend preservation of memory/numeric/atomic/authority/FFI facts, rejecting or retaining checks when preservation fails. Positive output witness: Checks-retained and optimized comparisons, exact proof/check identities and actual target preservation or residual check/rejection. Concrete negative case: Optimized execution erases a check without valid proof or a backend weakens memory/numeric/atomic/authority/FFI facts. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
