   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe16/report-production (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: claimed-profile safety corpus, actual compiler diagnostics/artifacts and target execution or explicit unavailable status. Required positive predicate: Emit machine-readable per-fixture conformance reports linking compiler/profile/target, expected/actual outcomes, diagnostics, inspected artifacts, proofs, islands and pass/fail for publication/release consumers. Positive output witness: Machine-readable per-fixture conformance report with all subject identities, inspections and honest pass/fail/unavailable status. Concrete negative case: A report omits compiler/profile/target, expected/actual verdict, diagnostic/artifact/proof/island IDs or marks unavailable/failed cases passing. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
