   :id "interface/safety/safe2/access-validity",
   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe2/access-validity (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: typed memory operation with storage/range/initialization/lifetime/alias/provider facts. Required positive predicate: Classify memory operations and accept safe access only when storage, initialization, bounds, lifetime, aliasing, synchronization, allocator, profile and capability facts hold; otherwise check, reject or audit explicitly. Positive output witness: Operation validity facts for storage, initialization, bounds, lifetime, alias, synchronization, allocator, profile and authority. Concrete negative case: A load has valid bounds but expired storage, an uninitialized range, wrong allocator or incompatible ownership/synchronization. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
