   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe2/checks (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: typed memory operation with storage/range/initialization/lifetime/alias/provider facts. Required positive predicate: Emit memory check records with profile-legal failure and declared allocation/blocking/host effects for dynamic bounds, null, initialization, lifetime, region, borrow, release, allocator and device checks. Positive output witness: Emitted memory checks, ordering before access, declared failure/effects and source/provider context. Concrete negative case: A dynamic lifetime/allocator/device check is recorded but omitted before access, or its failure blocks/allocates without declared effects. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
