   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe3/concurrent-transfer (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: owned/borrowed arguments, call contracts, lifetimes and escape destinations. Required positive predicate: Make task, actor and workflow ownership transfer explicit; permit sharing or borrowing only with valid synchronization and structured lifetime proof; reject detached local borrow capture. Positive output witness: Task/actor/workflow transfer, parent-consumption and structured lifetime/synchronization proof. Concrete negative case: A detached task captures a local borrow or the parent uses an owned value after moving it to an actor. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
