   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe4/arena-invalidation (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: region/arena allocation/reset graph with provider, generation and task/foreign lifetimes. Required positive predicate: On reset create a new arena generation and invalidate earlier values; prove absence of later use, emit supported generation checks or reject, while distinguishing region lifetime from arena identity/generation. Positive output witness: Arena identity/generation/reset edges, invalidation and proof or supported generation checks. Concrete negative case: An arena value from generation N is used after reset to N+1, or a region lifetime is mistaken for arena generation. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
