   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe7/generated-bindings (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: foreign declaration/call/callback and actual ABI/host/provider boundary. Required positive predicate: Emit source/generator digests, declarations, unsafe imports, wrappers, mappings and conformance records for generated bindings, rejecting raw unsafe exports without reviewed-safe metadata. Positive output witness: Generated source digest/version, declarations/imports/wrappers/type/error mappings and conformance provenance. Concrete negative case: Header/IDL/schema bindings export raw unsafe calls without source/generator digest, mappings, wrappers or audit. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
