   :criterion-texts
   ["Allocation interface/safety/safe8/race-prevention (Open). Role: legality compile-time safety/conformance checker. Input: task/shared-location/synchronization graph and selected target/provider memory model. Required positive predicate: Reject unsynchronized conflicting mutable accesses unless ownership, atomics, synchronization or checked provider ordering establishes safety, or explicitly audit unsafe behavior. Positive output witness: Conflicting-access graph, ownership/order evidence and safe/check/reject/explicit-unsafe outcome. Concrete negative case: Two tasks access the same mutable location with a write and no ownership/synchronization/atomic/provider ordering proof. Required refusal: this counterexample must not be accepted as ordinary safe behavior; retain only the governing proven-safe/runtime-checked/rejected/explicit-audited-unsafe alternatives and actual mode/profile exceptions. Evidence: inspect these actual output records and owning diagnostic IDs/source or generated-origin spans; record failed/unavailable/unrun cases, never turn a source fixture or manifest flag into execution acceptance. Dependencies: types/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/types5-integrate-typed-core supplies Actual typed core, ownership/layout and source-origin facts; effects/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/effects5-integrate-checked-core-consumers supplies Actual propagated effects and required capability facts; runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries supplies Source-qualified provider/runtime/domain safety result and exact consuming-boundary evidence; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Whole shared-facet entailment and implementation acceptance are not conferred."],
